@ Index:   Free-fall height residual for SOLVE
@ Height residual in Earth's gravity, set to zero by interactive
@ SOLVE: h0 + v0*time - g_⊕/2*time^2 - height.
@
@ Originally published as the function passed to SOLVE under
@ "The Solver" section of the WP43 Owner's Manual.
@
@ Author:  Walter Bonin, fm org C47 test program
@ Created: original publication date unknown
@ Version: 0.29
@ Tested: SOLVE time for height 0, h0=50, v0=15 returns 5.070303019685519581163707165121980 s.
@ input:  variables height=0, h0=50, v0=15; SOLVE time, guesses 5 and 10
@ output: time = 5.070303019685519581163707165121980 s
LBL ‘FreeF’
  MVAR ‘height’
  MVAR ‘h0’
  MVAR ‘v0’
  MVAR ‘time’
  g_⊕
  -2
  ÷
  RCL× ‘time’
  RCL+ ‘v0’
  RCL× ‘time’
  RCL+ ‘h0’
  RCL- ‘height’     ; residual of the height equation
  RTN
  END
.END.
